{"id":"mahabharata-3-277","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":277,"title":"सप्तसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 277 · The birth of Savitri","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks whether any woman was ever as devoted as Draupadi, and Markandeya tells of Savitri. King Ashvapati of Madra, childless, worships the goddess Savitri for eighteen years and is granted a daughter, whom he names Savitri; when she grows up and no suitor dares approach her, he sends her to choose a husband herself.","kn":"ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯಷ್ಟು ಪತಿನಿಷ್ಠೆಯ ಸ್ತ್ರೀ ಯಾರಾದರೂ ಇದ್ದಳೇ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಸಾವಿತ್ರಿಯ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಂತಾನಹೀನ ಮದ್ರರಾಜ ಅಶ್ವಪತಿ ಹದಿನೆಂಟು ವರ್ಷ ಸಾವಿತ್ರೀದೇವಿಯನ್ನು ಆರಾಧಿಸಿ ಮಗಳನ್ನು ಪಡೆದು ಸಾವಿತ್ರಿ ಎಂದು ಹೆಸರಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬೆಳೆದ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಯಾವ ವರನೂ ಸಮೀಪಿಸಲು ಧೈರ್ಯ ಮಾಡದಾಗ ತಾನೇ ಪತಿಯನ್ನು ಆರಿಸಲು ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि क्या कभी कोई स्त्री द्रौपदी जैसी पतिव्रता हुई, और मार्कण्डेय सावित्री की कथा सुनाते हैं। निःसन्तान मद्रराज अश्वपति अठारह वर्ष देवी सावित्री की उपासना कर एक पुत्री पाते हैं, जिसका नाम सावित्री रखते हैं; बड़ी होने पर जब कोई वर उसके पास आने का साहस नहीं करता, तो वे उसे स्वयं पति चुनने भेजते हैं।","te":"ద్రౌపదివంటి పతివ్రత ఎవరైనా ఉందా అని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడగగా మార్కండేయుడు సావిత్రి కథ చెబుతాడు. సంతానం లేని మద్రరాజు అశ్వపతి పద్దెనిమిదేళ్లు సావిత్రీదేవిని ఆరాధించి కుమార్తెను పొంది సావిత్రి అని పేరు పెడతాడు; పెరిగిన ఆమెను ఏ వరుడూ సమీపించే సాహసం చేయకపోవడంతో తానే భర్తను ఎంచుకోమని పంపుతాడు.","ta":"திரௌபதியைப் போல் கணவனிடம் பற்றுள்ள பெண் எவளேனும் இருந்தாளா என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, மார்க்கண்டேயர் ஸாவித்ரியின் கதையைச் சொல்கிறார். மக்கட்பேறற்ற மத்ர மன்னன் அஶ்வபதி பதினெட்டு ஆண்டுகள் ஸாவித்ரீ தேவியை வழிபட்டு ஒரு மகளைப் பெற்று ஸாவித்ரி எனப் பெயரிடுகிறான்; வளர்ந்த அவளை எந்த மணமகனும் அணுகத் துணியாததால் தானே கணவனைத் தேர்ந்தெடுக்க அனுப்புகிறான்.","ml":"ദ്രൗപദിയെപ്പോലെ വിശ്വസ്തയായ ഒരു സ്ത്രീ എപ്പോഴെങ്കിലും ഉണ്ടായിട്ടുണ്ടോ എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ സാവിത്രിയുടെ കഥ പറയുന്നു. മദ്രദേശത്തിലെ അശ്വപതി രാജാവ്, സന്താനമില്ലാതെ, സാവിത്രീദേവിയെ പതിനെട്ടു വർഷം ആരാധിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് ഒരു മകളെ വരമായി ലഭിക്കുന്നു; അവൾക്ക് സാവിത്രി എന്ന് പേരിടുന്നു. വളർന്നപ്പോൾ അവളെ സമീപിക്കാൻ ആരും ധൈര്യപ്പെടാത്തതിനാൽ, ഭർത്താവിനെ സ്വയം തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കാൻ അവളെ അയക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.277; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नात्मानमनुशोचामि नेमान्भ्रातॄन्महामुने ।\nहरणं चापि राज्यस्य यथेमां द्रुपदात्मजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, I do not grieve for myself, nor for these brothers, nor for the loss of the kingdom, as I do for this daughter of Drupada."}},{"n":2,"text":"द्यूते दुरात्मभिः क्लिष्टाः कृष्णया तारिता वयम् ।\nजयद्रथेन च पुनर्वनादपहृता बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Troubled at the dice by the wicked, we were rescued by Krishna; and then Jayadratha carried her off by force from the forest."}},{"n":3,"text":"अस्ति सीमन्तिनी काचिद्दृष्टपूर्वाथ वा श्रुता ।\nपतिव्रता महाभागा यथेयं द्रुपदात्मजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is there any woman, seen before or heard of, so faithful to her husband and so fortunate, as this daughter of Drupada?"}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"शृणु राजन्कुलस्त्रीणां महाभाग्यं युधिष्ठिर ।\nसर्वमेतद्यथा प्राप्तं सावित्र्या राजकन्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, Yudhishthira, the greatness of the women of good families, all of it as it came about in the case of the royal maiden Savitri."}},{"n":5,"text":"आसीन्मद्रेषु धर्मात्मा राजा परमधार्मिकः ।\nब्रह्मण्यश्च शरण्यश्च सत्यसंधो जितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the land of the Madras there was a righteous king, supremely dutiful, devoted to Brahmins, a protector of those who sought refuge, true to his word and master of his senses."}},{"n":6,"text":"यज्वा दानपतिर्दक्षः पौरजानपदप्रियः ।\nपार्थिवोऽश्वपतिर्नाम सर्वभूतहिते रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This king, named Ashvapati, was a sacrificer and a giver, skilled, loved by townspeople and countrymen, and devoted to the good of all beings."}},{"n":7,"text":"क्षमावाननपत्यश्च सत्यवाग्विजितेन्द्रियः ।\nअतिक्रान्तेन वयसा संतापमुपजग्मिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was patient, truthful, and self-controlled, but he had no child, and as his age passed he fell into sorrow."}},{"n":8,"text":"अपत्योत्पादनार्थं स तीव्रं नियममास्थितः ।\nकाले परिमिताहारो ब्रह्मचारी जितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To obtain offspring he took up a strict discipline, eating a measured amount at the proper times, living as a celibate, with his senses under control."}},{"n":9,"text":"हुत्वा शतसहस्रं स सावित्र्या राजसत्तम ।\nषष्ठे षष्ठे तदा काले बभूव मितभोजनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, he offered a hundred thousand oblations with the Savitri mantra, taking a measured meal only at the sixth meal time in each period."}},{"n":10,"text":"एतेन नियमेनासीद्वर्षाण्यष्टादशैव तु ।\nपूर्णे त्वष्टादशे वर्षे सावित्री तुष्टिमभ्यगात् ।\nस्वरूपिणी तदा राजन्दर्शयामास तं नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He kept this discipline for eighteen years, and when the eighteenth year was complete, Savitri was pleased and appeared to the king in bodily form."}},{"n":11,"text":"अग्निहोत्रात्समुत्थाय हर्षेण महतान्विता ।\nउवाच चैनं वरदा वचनं पार्थिवं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rising from the agnihotra fire with great joy, the boon-giver spoke to the king:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ब्रह्मचर्येण शुद्धेन दमेन नियमेन च ।\nसर्वात्मना च मद्भक्त्या तुष्टास्मि तव पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased with you, king, for your pure celibacy, self-restraint, discipline, and your devotion to me with all your being."}},{"n":13,"text":"वरं वृणीष्वाश्वपते मद्रराज यथेप्सितम् ।\nन प्रमादश्च धर्मेषु कर्तव्यस्ते कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Choose a boon as you wish, Ashvapati, king of the Madras; but you must never be careless in your duties.\""}},{"text":"अश्वपतिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashvapati said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अपत्यार्थः समारम्भः कृतो धर्मेप्सया मया ।\nपुत्रा मे बहवो देवि भवेयुः कुलभावनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I undertook this effort for the sake of children, wishing to fulfill dharma. Goddess, may I have many sons who will uphold my family."}},{"n":15,"text":"तुष्टासि यदि मे देवि काममेतं वृणोम्यहम् ।\nसंतानं हि परो धर्म इत्याहुर्मां द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you are pleased with me, goddess, this is the wish I choose. The twice-born tell me that offspring is the highest dharma.\""}},{"text":"सावित्र्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Savitri said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"पूर्वमेव मया राजन्नभिप्रायमिमं तव ।\nज्ञात्वा पुत्रार्थमुक्तो वै तव हेतोः पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, I already knew this intention of yours and spoke to the Grandfather on your behalf for sons."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रसादाच्चैव तस्मात्ते स्वयंभुविहिताद्भुवि ।\nकन्या तेजस्विनी सौम्य क्षिप्रमेव भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"By his favor, ordained by the Self-born, a radiant daughter will soon be born to you on earth, gentle one."}},{"n":18,"text":"उत्तरं च न ते किंचिद्व्याहर्तव्यं कथंचन ।\nपितामहनिसर्गेण तुष्टा ह्येतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You must not reply to this in any way; I tell you this, pleased by the decision of the Grandfather.\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"स तथेति प्रतिज्ञाय सावित्र्या वचनं नृपः ।\nप्रसादयामास पुनः क्षिप्रमेवं भवेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king agreed, saying \"So be it,\" to Savitri's words, and again begged her, \"May it happen quickly.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"अन्तर्हितायां सावित्र्यां जगाम स्वगृहं नृपः ।\nस्वराज्ये चावसत्प्रीतः प्रजा धर्मेण पालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Savitri had vanished, the king went to his own house, and lived happily in his kingdom, protecting his subjects with dharma."}},{"n":21,"text":"कस्मिंश्चित्तु गते काले स राजा नियतव्रतः ।\nज्येष्ठायां धर्मचारिण्यां महिष्यां गर्भमादधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"After some time, the king, firm in his vows, conceived a child in his eldest wife, who was devoted to dharma."}},{"n":22,"text":"राजपुत्र्यां तु गर्भः स मालव्यां भरतर्षभ ।\nव्यवर्धत यथा शुक्ले तारापतिरिवाम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That embryo in the princess from Malava grew, best of the Bharatas, as the moon grows in the bright fortnight in the sky."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्राप्ते काले तु सुषुवे कन्यां राजीवलोचनाम् ।\nक्रियाश्च तस्या मुदितश्चक्रे स नृपतिस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the right time she gave birth to a lotus-eyed daughter, and the king, delighted, performed the rites for her."}},{"n":24,"text":"सावित्र्या प्रीतया दत्ता सावित्र्या हुतया ह्यपि ।\nसावित्रीत्येव नामास्याश्चक्रुर्विप्रास्तथा पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since she was given by the pleased Savitri and born from oblations with the Savitri mantra, the Brahmins and her father named her Savitri."}},{"n":25,"text":"सा विग्रहवतीव श्रीर्व्यवर्धत नृपात्मजा ।\nकालेन चापि सा कन्या यौवनस्था बभूव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king's daughter grew up like Shri, the goddess of fortune, in a body, and in time she reached youth."}},{"n":26,"text":"तां सुमध्यां पृथुश्रोणीं प्रतिमां काञ्चनीमिव ।\nप्राप्तेयं देवकन्येति दृष्ट्वा संमेनिरे जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her slim-waisted, broad-hipped, like a golden statue, people thought, \"A daughter of the gods has come.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तां तु पद्मपलाशाक्षीं ज्वलन्तीमिव तेजसा ।\nन कश्चिद्वरयामास तेजसा प्रतिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But no one asked for that lotus-eyed girl, who seemed to blaze with brightness, kept off by her radiance."}},{"n":28,"text":"अथोपोष्य शिरःस्नाता दैवतान्यभिगम्य सा ।\nहुत्वाग्निं विधिवद्विप्रान्वाचयामास पर्वणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then she fasted, bathed her head, visited the gods, offered oblations in the fire as the rule says, and had Brahmins recite blessings on the holy day."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः सुमनसः शेषाः प्रतिगृह्य महात्मनः ।\nपितुः सकाशमगमद्देवी श्रीरिव रूपिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the remaining flowers from the offering, the lady, like Shri in person, went to her great-souled father."}},{"n":30,"text":"साभिवाद्य पितुः पादौ शेषाः पूर्वं निवेद्य च ।\nकृताञ्जलिर्वरारोहा नृपतेः पार्श्वतः स्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saluted her father's feet, presented the remaining flowers, and stood with joined hands at the king's side, lovely-hipped."}},{"n":31,"text":"यौवनस्थां तु तां दृष्ट्वा स्वां सुतां देवरूपिणीम् ।\nअयाच्यमानां च वरैर्नृपतिर्दुःखितोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his own daughter, godlike in form and grown to youth, and not sought by any suitors, the king was sad."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"पुत्रि प्रदानकालस्ते न च कश्चिद्वृणोति माम् ।\nस्वयमन्विच्छ भर्तारं गुणैः सदृशमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Daughter, it is time for you to be given in marriage, and no one asks for you. Seek for yourself a husband equal to you in qualities."}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रार्थितः पुरुषो यश्च स निवेद्यस्त्वया मम ।\nविमृश्याहं प्रदास्यामि वरय त्वं यथेप्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me of the man you choose; I will consider and give you. Choose as you wish."}},{"n":34,"text":"श्रुतं हि धर्मशास्त्रे मे पठ्यमानं द्विजातिभिः ।\nतथा त्वमपि कल्याणि गदतो मे वचः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have heard from the twice-born reciting the law books, and you too, auspicious one, hear what I say:"}},{"n":35,"text":"अप्रदाता पिता वाच्यो वाच्यश्चानुपयन्पतिः ।\nमृते भर्तरि पुत्रश्च वाच्यो मातुररक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"A father who does not give his daughter in marriage is to be blamed; a husband who does not approach his wife is to be blamed; and a son who does not protect his mother after her husband's death is to be blamed."}},{"n":36,"text":"इदं मे वचनं श्रुत्वा भर्तुरन्वेषणे त्वर ।\nदेवतानां यथा वाच्यो न भवेयं तथा कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words of mine, make haste to look for a husband, and act so that I may not be blamed by the gods.\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा दुहितरं तथा वृद्धांश्च मन्त्रिणः ।\nव्यादिदेशानुयात्रं च गम्यतामित्यचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to his daughter and to his old ministers, he ordered her an escort and urged her, \"Go.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"साभिवाद्य पितुः पादौ व्रीडितेव मनस्विनी ।\nपितुर्वचनमाज्ञाय निर्जगामाविचारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saluted her father's feet, as if shy, and, understanding her father's word, went out without hesitation."}},{"n":39,"text":"सा हैमं रथमास्थाय स्थविरैः सचिवैर्वृता ।\nतपोवनानि रम्याणि राजर्षीणां जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting a golden chariot, surrounded by aged ministers, she went to the lovely penance groves of the royal sages."}},{"n":40,"text":"मान्यानां तत्र वृद्धानां कृत्वा पादाभिवन्दनम् ।\nवनानि क्रमशस्तात सर्वाण्येवाभ्यगच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There she bowed at the feet of the revered elders, and, dear Yudhishthira, went through all the forests in turn."}},{"n":41,"text":"एवं सर्वेषु तीर्थेषु धनोत्सर्गं नृपात्मजा ।\nकुर्वती द्विजमुख्यानां तं तं देशं जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"So at all the holy places the king's daughter gave away wealth to the best of the twice-born, and went to each region."}}]}]}